Measure a headless terminal through its snapshot channel and report every result.

The upstream driver and test methods still run on the terminal pty. Only
screen inspection uses the optional channel; direct protocol queries keep
their original path. DA1 checks the declared VT220/color profile rather than
xterm build options. An erased cell is expected empty, as an unwritten one
is, since libtsm keeps no blank apart from an empty cell, which xterm's
checksum does. A final count detects interrupted or empty runs.
Each test begins by sending CAN and XTVERSION and discarding what the
terminal sends before XTVERSION's reply, so that a reply or string a failed
test left behind cannot fail the tests after it.

